  "faq": [
    {
      "question": "What is Svíčková?",
      "answer": "Svíčková na smetaně is a traditional Czech dish. It's a sirloin steak braised in a vegetable cream sauce, typically served with bread dumplings (houskové knedlíky), a slice of lemon, whipped cream, and cranberry sauce. It's a staple of Czech cuisine and a must-try when visiting."
    },
    {
      "question": "How much does Svíčková cost in Prague?",
      "answer": "A plate of Svíčková in a restaurant in Prague typically costs between 250 and 450 Kč ($10-$19 USD). More upscale restaurants might charge more, while local pubs (hospoda) or cafeterias (jídelna) may offer it for less, especially as a lunch special."
    },
    {
      "question": "What do you drink with Svíčková?",
      "answer": "The classic pairing for Svíčková is a cold, crisp Czech pilsner beer. The bitterness of the beer cuts through the richness of the creamy sauce perfectly. For a non-alcoholic option, Kofola, a traditional Czech soft drink, is also a popular choice."
    }
  ],
